MODIFICATIONS, per section 3(b) of the Agreement

The files here are NOT the upstream files. Each was changed, as follows.

  * `qwenimage21_*.json` are graph exports traced out of the Diffusers and
    Transformers implementations into JuliaVision's own operator format: the
    transformer, text encoder and VAE decoder by `tools/export_qwenimage21.py`,
    and for reference images the vision tower, the language model with
    multimodal positions, the VAE encoder, and the transformer split into
    prefix segments and a cached denoising step by
    `tools/export_qwenimage21_condition.py`. They describe the upstream
    model's structure and carry no weights.

  * `*_constants.safetensors` hold tensors the export lifted out of the
    traced graphs -- rotary frequency tables, selection masks and the timestep
    frequency table -- computed from the upstream configuration.

  * `vae.safetensors` is the upstream VAE at its own single precision,
    renamed to the exported graphs' buffer names.

  * In the test-fixture artifact, `*.safetensors` other than the weights are
    activations computed by running the model on generated inputs, and
    `smoke_*` are the same graph exports taken from a small randomly
    initialised model with the upstream architecture.

  * `weights-<i>of<n>.safetensors` are Comfy-Org's quantized checkpoints --
    themselves a modification of Qwen's released weights -- split into pieces
    that fit a release asset. The split is byte-for-byte: concatenating the
    tensors of all `n` pieces reproduces Comfy-Org's file exactly, and no
    value was altered. Comfy-Org's own quantization (tensor-wise INT8 with
    ConvRot for the denoiser, asymmetric W4A8 for the encoder) is a change to
    the upstream weights and is described at the compact checkpoint's page.

  * `processor/` is Qwen's tokenizer and chat template, copied unchanged.


